Dear Steve,
Feel free to contact me off the list and give some more details of the design you are using, in particular how transects are arranged over space and time. There are various options either with or without bootstrapping. The key step is to determine a conceptual framework in which the notion of 'significant change' makes sense: this framework will depend upon your spatiotemporal design. The scheme in Fewster et al (2000) is somewhat specific to the design it was applied to.

Best wishes,
Rachel

